sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: docs/cli/instance.mdx#orbit-instancerename (Swamp reads the checkout, the Gateway records the branch after success), ADR 0244 task, R2-R4; DECISIONS instance.rename as corrected 2026-11-02 (keep the Swamp read of HEAD; Node agent observations later, in the observer pass); DECISIONS 2 (DNS held).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:rename
  %% kind: instance.rename
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: instance:rename 42<br/>--branch=t3code/login-redirect
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:rename 42 --branch=t3code/login-redirect`
  %%> - syntax: `instance:rename <instance> --branch=BRANCH [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - a local branch you already checked out, for example after `git branch -m t3code/login-redirect`
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - it does not rename the Instance, move its directory or change Git `HEAD`
  %%> - `--domain` returns `operation.kind_unavailable`
  Note over GW: Validate, record intent<br/>Instance 42 · task #5160
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - Instance 42 is an active development checkout on Node 12
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - the branch is a valid local branch name
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5160 recorded with the full intent; nothing is recorded on the Instance yet
  %%> Later:
  %%> - in the observer pass, the Gateway checks the Node agent's checkout facts and records the branch with no run
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-rename
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> - the checkout path, its recorded identity and the requested branch
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5160
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Read the checkout<br/>@swamp/ssh · top, origin, HEAD
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks the checkout's top level, common Git directory, worktrees and origin against its recorded identity
  %%> - reads symbolic `HEAD` and its commit
  %%> How:
  %%> - Git commands run with hooks and filesystem monitors off, with no origin access
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - changes nothing on the Node; a dirty or unpublished branch can be recorded
  alt HEAD names the branch
    N-->>SW: branch, commit
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the checked-out branch and its commit
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the branch<br/>selected_branch · override
    %%> Result:
    %%> - `selected_branch` and `branch_override` of Instance 42 become `t3code/login-redirect`
    %%> - recording the already recorded branch keeps its existing override
    %%> - task #5160 succeeds
  else not checked out or identity changed
    N--xSW: other branch or detached
    %%> When:
    %%> - symbolic `HEAD` names another branch or is detached
    %%> - or the checkout no longer matches its recorded identity
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Record nothing<br/>task failed · rerun is safe
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Instance 42 keeps its recorded branch; task #5160 fails
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - check out the branch, then run `instance:rename` again; it is a new task
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5160
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
